&lt;p&gt;No, because this code created to become a part of 3.0. &lt;br/&gt;
It is not good idea to restrict atomic ops now, this can cause issues at customers deployments.&lt;br/&gt;
Currently we allow atomic ops, but already restricted them at tests.&lt;br/&gt;
So, allow() now useful at tests.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At 3.0 we&apos;ll disable atomic ops by default.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So, there is no need to have disallow() method.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16523744" author="dpavlov" created="Tue, 26 Jun 2018 13:50:35 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=avinogradov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;avinogradov&quot;&gt;avinogradov&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=SomeFire&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;SomeFire&quot;&gt;SomeFire&lt;/a&gt;, thank you for explaining, I understood now.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I&apos;ve merged changes to master.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
