                            <comment id="16523866" author="dpavlov" created="Tue, 26 Jun 2018 15:28:48 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=SomeFire&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;SomeFire&quot;&gt;SomeFire&lt;/a&gt;, thank you &lt;img class=&quot;emoticon&quot; src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/images/icons/emoticons/smile.png&quot; height=&quot;16&quot; width=&quot;16&quot; align=&quot;absmiddle&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; border=&quot;0&quot;/&gt; Looking forward to your new contributions.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16526494" author="agoncharuk" created="Thu, 28 Jun 2018 16:32:59 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=SomeFire&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;SomeFire&quot;&gt;SomeFire&lt;/a&gt;, apparently, the change does not work - the method &lt;tt&gt;withAllowAtomicOpsInTx&lt;/tt&gt; itself throws an exception if it is called on an atomic cache.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Can you estimate how long a fix will take? If it takes more than a day, I will have to revert the change.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16526526" author="somefire" created="Thu, 28 Jun 2018 16:52:10 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=agoncharuk&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;agoncharuk&quot;&gt;agoncharuk&lt;/a&gt;, it throws exception only inside transaction, so to use it we must call &lt;tt&gt;withAllowAtomicOpsInTx&lt;/tt&gt;&#160;before transaction.&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16527361" author="avinogradov" created="Fri, 29 Jun 2018 09:36:52 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=SomeFire&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;SomeFire&quot;&gt;SomeFire&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What about to make some patch to restrict withAllowAtomicOpsInTx call inside tx?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
